BUNDLED BINARY: native/prebuilt/x64/DfxBridge.dll
=================================================

str-amp ships a prebuilt DfxBridge.dll so that a normal build needs no C++ toolchain.
It contains FxSound's DSP library and the flat C entry points in native/dfxbridge, and
is covered by the AGPL like the rest of this project.

The AGPL requires that the corresponding source be available to anyone who receives the
binary. It is:

  * The bridge source is native/dfxbridge/ in this repository.
  * FxSound's source is https://github.com/fxsound2/fxsound-app
    The shipped binary was built from commit aed079771554b47766a750e7f181f75b7808108a.

The FxSound source is used with one change, which the AGPL requires be published along with
the binary. It is native/dfxbridge/fxsound-registry-namespace.patch, and it renames the
registry key the library keeps its live settings under, from "DFX" to "StrAmp".

That matters because the library reads those settings on startup and writes them back as it
runs. Left unchanged, str-amp would share one set of live settings with an installed FxSound
on the same machine, reading that install's state and overwriting it. Measured before the
change, str-amp picked up an FxSound install's all-effects-off state and a preset that should
have added 4.4 dB added 0.5 dB instead. After it, the FxSound tree is untouched byte for byte.
The patch also removes a MessageBox the library raises if it fails to start, which would block
on a thread with no message loop to dismiss it.

To rebuild it (Visual Studio 2022, x64):

  git clone https://github.com/fxsound2/fxsound-app
  cd fxsound-app
  git checkout aed079771554b47766a750e7f181f75b7808108a
  git apply <str-amp>\native\dfxbridge\fxsound-registry-namespace.patch
  msbuild dsp\DfxDsp.vcxproj -p:Configuration=Release -p:Platform=x64

  cd <str-amp>\native\dfxbridge
  msbuild DfxBridge.vcxproj -p:Configuration=Release -p:Platform=x64 ^
          -p:FxSoundRoot=<path to fxsound-app>

  copy build\x64\DfxBridge.dll ..\prebuilt\x64\

DfxDsp.vcxproj builds a static library, and DfxBridge links it together with the utility
modules from audiopassthru that it depends on, so the result is one self-contained DLL
with no runtime dependency on an FxSound installation.
